# Dotfiles installed into $HOME — the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the file set,
# read by both install.sh and provision/steps/60-shell.sh (so the two can't drift).
# One repo-relative path per line; it mirrors the same path under $HOME.
# Entries may be files OR directories (a dir is linked/copied whole).
# Blank lines and #-comments are ignored.
#
# How they're installed is the caller's choice:
#   - symlink (default): repo is the source of truth; editing ~/<file> edits the
#     repo copy. Requires the repo to stay at its path.
#   - copy / override (DOTFILES_COPY=1, or GOLDEN_IMAGE=1, or install.sh --copy):
#     self-contained; the repo can be deleted afterwards, but edits no longer
#     flow back to the repo.
.zshrc
.p10k.zsh
.gitconfig
.tmux.conf
.config/alacritty/alacritty.toml
.config/nvim
.claude/settings.json
.claude/statusline-command.sh
